"Discussiones Mathematicae (https://bibliotekanauki.pl/articles/59882303.pdf)\nciteturn0search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; Discussiones Mathematicae ... on eﬃcient dominating sets is given and optimal equitable 4-colorings are ... Keywords: Pancake graph, chromatic number, equitable coloring.\nDiscussiones Mathematicae\nGraph Theory 44 (2024) 35–46\nhttps://doi.org/10.7151/dmgt.2432\nAN IMPROVED BOUND ON THE CHROMATIC NUMBER\nOF THE PANCAKE GRAPHS\nLeen Droogendijk\nand\nElena V. Konstantinova\nSobolev Institute of Mathematics, Novosibirsk, 630090, Russia\nNovosibirsk State University, Novosibirsk, 630090, Russia\ne-mail: drooge001@kpnmail.nl\ne konsta@math.nsc.ru\nAbstract\nIn this paper, an improved bound on the chromatic number of the Pan-\ncake graph Pn, n ⩾9, is presented. The bound is obtained using a subad-\nditivity property of the chromatic number of the Pancake graph. We also\ninvestigate an equitable coloring of Pn. An equitable (n −1)-coloring based\non eﬃcient dominating sets is given and optimal equitable 4-colorings are\nconsidered for small n. It is conjectured that the chromatic number of Pn\ncoincides with its equitable chromatic number for any n ⩾2.\nKeywords: Pancake graph, chromatic number, equitable coloring.\n2020 Mathematics Subject Classiﬁcation: 05C15, 05C25, 05C69.\n1.\nIntroduction\nThe Pancake graph Pn, n ⩾2, is deﬁned as the Cayley graph over the symmetric\ngroup Symn with the generating set of all preﬁx-reversals ri, 2 ⩽i ⩽n, inverting\nthe order of any initial substring of length 1 · · · i of a permutation when multiplied\non the right. It is a connected, vertex-transitive, (n −1)-regular graph without\nloops and multiple edges of order n!. It contains all cycles Cl of length l, where\n6 ⩽l ⩽n! [15, 25].\nA mapping c : V (Γ) →{1, 2, . . . , k} is called a proper k-coloring of a graph\nΓ = (V, E) if c(u) ̸= c(v) whenever the vertices u and v are adjacent.\nThe\nchromatic number χ(Γ) of a graph Γ is the least number of colors needed to--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAn extension on neighbor sum distinguishing total coloring of graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.02781)\nciteturn0academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.8 years ago; The smallest value $k$ for which $G$ has such a coloring is called the neighbor full sum distinguishing total chromatic number of $G$ and denoted by fgndi$_{\\sum}(G)$. ... In this paper we conjecture that fgndi$_{\\sum}(G)\\leq 3$ for any connected graph $G$ of order at least three.\nTitle: An extension on neighbor sum distinguishing total coloring of graphs\nAuthors: Jing-zhi Chang, Chao Yang, Zhi-xiang Yin, Bing Yao\nDate: Sat Jan  8 07:01:27 2022\n\nLet $f: V(G)\\cup E(G)\\rightarrow \\{1,2,\\dots,k\\}$ be a non-proper total $k$-coloring of $G$. Define a weight function on total coloring as $$\\phi(x)=f(x)+\\sum\\limits_{e\\ni x}f(e)+\\sum\\limits_{y\\in N(x)}f(y),$$ where $N(x)=\\{y\\in V(G)|xy\\in E(G)\\}$. If $\\phi(x)\\neq \\phi(y)$ for any edge $xy\\in E(G)$, then $f$ is called a neighbor full sum distinguishing total $k$-coloring of $G$. The smallest value $k$ for which $G$ has such a coloring is called the neighbor full sum distinguishing total chromatic number of $G$ and denoted by fgndi$_{\\sum}(G)$. The coloring is an extension of neighbor sum distinguishing non-proper total coloring. In this paper we conjecture that fgndi$_{\\sum}(G)\\leq 3$ for any connected graph $G$ of order at least three. We prove that the conjecture is true for (i) paths and cycles; (ii) 3-regular graphs and (iii) stars, complete graphs, trees, hypercubes, bipartite graphs and complete $r$-partite graphs. In particular, complete graphs can achieve the upper bound for the above conjecture.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn a total version of 1-2-3 Conjecture (https://bibliotekanauki.pl/articles/31348090.pdf)\nciteturn0search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Since \\(G\\) is regular, it follows that \\(G\\) admits a neighbor full sum distinguishing total 3-coloring.\n1182 O. Baudon, H. Hocquard, A. Marczyk, M. Pilśniak, J. Przybyło ...\n\n3-coloring of \\(K_n\\). Since the sum of colors of the vertices belonging to the closed neighborhood of any vertex of \\(K_n\\) is the same and equals \\(n\\). Hence, we cannot color the vertices and the edges in a desired manner using just two colors (such a coloring would imply the existence of an irregular assignment of \\(K_n\\)). Thus, the following proposition holds.\n\n**Proposition 13.** For \\(n \\ge 3\\), \\(\\chi^{ven}(K_n)=3\\).\n\nLet \\(K_r(t)\\) denote a complete \\(r\\)-partite graph with \\(t\\) vertices in each class (\\(r, t \\ge 1\\)). Faudree *et al.* [6] proved that if \\(G = K_r(t)\\), \\(r > 2\\) and \\(t \\ge 1\\), then \\(s(K_r(t)) = 3\\). Since \\(G\\) is regular, it follows that \\(G\\) admits a neighbor full sum distinguishing total 3-coloring.\n\n**Proposition 14.** If \\(r \\ge 3\\) and \\(t \\ge 1\\), then \\(\\chi^{ven}(K_r(t)) \\le 3\\).\n\nIn [10] the authors studied a coloring of the edges of the graph with the elements of an abelian group.\n\n**Theorem 15** [10]. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n限制最大平均度下图的邻点全和可区别全染色* (https://xuebaozr.sysu.edu.cn/rc-pub/front/front-article/download/133318673/lowqualitypdf/Neighbor%20full%20sum%20distinguishing%20total%20coloring%20of%20graphs%20with%20bounded%20maximum%20average%20degree.pdf)\nciteturn0search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; By the way, it further follows that the conjecture (Cui et al., 2023) of neighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring holds on graphs with Δ(G)≥7 and mad(G)<7/3.\n第65卷 第1期  \n2026年1月  \n中山大学学报（自然科学版中英文）  \nACTA SCIENTIARUM NATURALIUM UNIVERSITATIS SUNYATSENI  \nVol. 65 No. 1  \nJan. 2026  \nDOI: 10.13471/j.cnki.acta.snus.ZR20240354\n\n限制最大平均度下图的邻点全和可区别全染色*\n\n李志军，文飞，岳忠政\n\n兰州交通大学应用数学研究所，甘肃 兰州 730070\n\n**摘 要：**图G的邻点全和可区别全染色是一个满足任意两个相邻顶点的全和不同的正常染色，其中顶点的全和是该点及其关联元素所染的颜色之和。将所用的最少颜色数称为G的邻点全和可区别全色数，记为 ftdniΣ(G)。设 mad(G) 和 Δ(G) 分别表示图G的最大平均度和最大度，运用组合零点定理与权转移法得到：(i) 若 Δ(G)=3 且 mad(G)<12/5，则 ftdniΣ(G)≤6；(ii) 若 Δ(G)=4 且 mad(G)<11/5，则 ftdniΣ(G)≤8；(iii) 若 Δ(G)≥5 且 mad(G)<7/3，则 ftdniΣ(G)≤max{9, Δ(G)+2}。从而推知，当图G满足 Δ(G)≥7 且 mad(G)<7/3 时，邻点全和可区别染色猜想（崔福祥等，2023）是成立的。\n\n**关键词：**正常全染色；邻点全和可区别全染色；最大平均度；组合零点定理  \n**中图分类号：**O157.5　**文献标志码：**A　**文章编号：**2097-0137(2026)01-0135-09\n\nNeighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring of graphs  \nwith bounded maximum average degree\n\nLI Zhijun，WEN Fei，YUE Zhongzheng\n\nInstitute of Applied Mathematics，Lanzhou Jiaotong University，Lanzhou 730070，China\n\n**Abstract:** A neighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring of a graph G is a proper total-coloring such that no two adjacent vertices meet the same full sum, where the full sum of a vertex consists of all colors assigned on the vertex and its incident elements, the minimum number of the colors required is called the neighbor full sum distinguishing total chromatic number, denoted by ftdniΣ(G). Let mad(G) and Δ(G) denote the maximum average degree and the maximum degree of graph G, respectively. In this paper, we prove the following results. (i) If G is a graph with Δ(G)=3 and mad(G)<12/5, then ftdniΣ(G)≤6. (ii) If G is a graph with Δ(G)=4 and mad(G)<11/5, then ftdniΣ(G)≤8. (iii) If G is a graph with Δ(G)≥5 and mad(G)<7/3, then ftdniΣ(G)≤max{9, Δ(G)+2}. By the way, it further follows that the conjecture (Cui et al., 2023) of neighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring holds on graphs with Δ(G)≥7 and mad(G)<7/3.\n\n**Key words:** proper total coloring; neighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring; maximum average degree; combinatorial nullstellensatz\n\n* 收稿日期: 2024-12-17　　录用日期: 2025-09-02　　网络首发日期: 2025-11-06  \n基金项目: 国家自然科学基金(12261055); 甘肃省自然科学基金重点项目(24JRRA222)  \n作者简介: 李志军(1998年生), 男; 研究方向: 图染色; E-mail: lzj12282023@163.com  \n通信作者: 文飞(1984年生), 男; 研究方向: 图染色、图谱理论; E-mail: wenfei@lzjtu.edu.cn\