aphs and complete r $ r $ -partite graphs. Meanwhile they posed a conjecture on NFSD-total coloring as follow:\n\nConjecture 1.3. ^{[5]} For any connected graph G $ G $ of order at least 3 $ 3 $, fgndi _{\\sum}(G)\\leq 3 $ _{\\sum}(G)\\leq 3 $.\n\nA Halin graph is a plane graph H $ H $ which constructed as follows. Let T $ T $ be a tree having at least 4 vertices, called the characteristic tree of H $ H $. All vertices of T $ T $ are either of degree 1, called leaves, or of degree at least 3. Let C $ C $ be a cycle, called the adjoint cycle of H $ H $, connecting all leaves of T $ T $ in such a way that C $ C $ forms the boundary of the unbounded face. We usually write H = T\\cup C $ H = T\\cup C $ to reveal the characteristic tree and the adjoint cycle. Let V_0\\subseteq V(H)\\setminus V(C) $ V_0\\subseteq V(H)\\setminus V(C) $ and each vertex in V_0 $ V_0 $ is adjacent to some vertices on C $ C $.\n\nThis paper is organized as follows. In Section 2, by induction on the length of the adjoint cycle C $ C $, we get that fgndi _{\\sum}(H)\\leq 3 $ _{\\sum}(H)\\leq 3 $ for any 3-regular Halin graph H $ H $. In Section 3, for a Halin graph H $ H $ with maximum degree \\Delta(H)\\geq 4 $ \\Delta(H)\\geq 4 $, if every vertex in V_0 $ V_0 $ has degree at least four, via a coloring algorithm of tree T $ T $ and by assigning colors to the edges of cycle C $ C $, we have fgndi _{\\sum}(H)\\leq 3 $ _{\\sum}(H)\\leq 3 $. Therefore, Conjecture 1.3 is valid for the above two types of Halin graphs.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n限制最大平均度下图的邻点全和可区别全染色. (https://openurl.ebsco.com/contentitem/doi%3A10.13471%2Fj.cnki.acta.snus.ZR20240354?id=ebsco%3Adoi%3A10.13471%2Fj.cnki.acta.snus.ZR20240354&sid=ebsco%3Aplink%3Acrawler)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: last week; By the way, it further follows that the conjecture（Cui et al., 2023） of neighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring holds on graphs with Δ (G) ≥ 7 and mad(G) <7/3.\n\n# 限制最大平均度下图的邻点全和可区别全染色.\n\nBy: 李志军; 文飞; 岳忠政 Published in: Acta Scientiarum Naturalium Universitatis Sunyatseni / Zhongshan Daxue Xuebao, 2026, v. 65, n. 1, p. 135, doi. 10.13471/j.cnki.acta.snus.ZR20240354\n\nAbstract\n    \n\n## A neighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring of a graph G is a proper total-coloring such that no two adjacent vertices meet the same full sum, where the full sum of a vertex consists of all colors assigned on the vertex and its incident elements, the minimum number of the colors required is called the neighbor full sum distinguishing total chromatic number, denoted by ftndiΣ (G). Let mad(G) and Δ (G) denote the maximum average degree and the maximum degree of graph G, respectively. In this paper, we prove the following results. （i） If G is a graph with Δ (G) = 3 and mad(G) < 12 5, then ftndiΣ (G) ≤ 6. （ii） If G is a graph with Δ (G) = 4 and mad(G) < 11 5, then ftndiΣ (G) ≤ 8. （iii） If G is a graph with Δ (G) ≥ 5 and mad(G) <73, then ftndiΣ (G) ≤ max {9, Δ (G) 2 }. By the way, it further follows that the conjecture（Cui et al., 2023） of neighbor full sum distinguishing total coloring holds on graphs with Δ (G) ≥ 7 and mad(G) <7/3.\n\nSubjects\n    \n\n## Graph coloring; Graph theory; Graph connectivity\n\nPublication\n    \n\n## Acta Scientiarum Naturalium Universitatis Sunyatseni / Zhongshan Daxue Xuebao, 2026, Vol 65, Issue 1, p135\n\nISSN\n    \n\n## 2097-0137\n\nPublication type\n    \n\n## Academic Journal\n\nDOI\n    \n\n## 10.13471/j.cnki.acta.snus.ZR20240354--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAn improved bound on the chromatic number of the Pancake graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.11092)\nciteturn0academia17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.6 years ago; In this paper an improved bound on the chromatic number of the Pancake graph $P_n, n\\geqslant 2$, is presented. ... An equitable $(n-1)$-coloring based on efficient dominating sets is given and optimal equitable $4$-colorings are considered for small $n$.\nTitle: An improved bound on the chromatic number of the Pancake graphs\nAuthors: Leen Droogendijk, Elena V. Konstantinova\nDate: Sat Mar 20 04:24:22 2021\n\nIn this paper an improved bound on the chromatic number of the Pancake graph $P_n, n\\geqslant 2$, is presented. The bound is obtained using a subadditivity property of the chromatic number of the Pancake graph. We also investigate an equitable coloring of $P_n$. An equitable $(n-1)$-coloring based on efficient dominating sets is given and optimal equitable $4$-colorings are considered for small $n$. It is conjectured that the chromatic number of $P_n$ coincides with its equitable chromatic number for any $n\\geqslant 2$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZhi-xiang Yin - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/author/zhi-xiang-yin)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; The smallest value $k$ for which $G$ has such a coloring is called the neighbor full sum distinguishing total chromatic number of $G$ and denoted by fgndi$_{\\sum}(G)$. ... Meanwhile, we show that every 3-regular graph can achieve a neighbor sum distinguishing edge coloring by using 4 colors, which answers 1-2-3 Conjecture positively.\n\n## Papers by Zhi-xiang Yin\n\n2 paper(s) by this author · All BibTeX\n\n2022-01-08\n\nJing-zhi Chang, Chao Yang, Zhi-xiang Yin, Bing Yao\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nAn extension on neighbor sum distinguishing total coloring of graphs\n\nLet $f: V(G)\\cup E(G)\\rightarrow \\{1,2,\\dots,k\\}$ be a non-proper total $k$-coloring of $G$. Define a weight function on total coloring as $$φ(x)=f(x)+\\sum\\limits_{e\\ni x}f(e)+\\sum\\limits_{y\\in N(x)}f(y),$$ where $N(x)=\\{y\\in V(G)|xy\\in E(G)\\}$. If $φ(x)\\neq φ(y)$ for any edge $xy\\in E(G)$, then $f$ is called a neighbor full sum distinguishing total $k$-coloring of $G$. The smallest value $k$ for which $G$ has such a 